<title>ROMANIA: Romania issues 2.66 trln lei in T-bills in Jan.</title>
<headline>Romania issues 2.66 trln lei in T-bills in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's Finance Ministry said on Wednesday it would offer 2.665 trillion lei worth of treasury bills this month to cover maturing papers.</p>
<p>The floating rate T-bills will be placed by the central bank through public subscriptions. Their annual yield will be calculated at the average of the weekly auctioned credit rates during the life period of the papers.</p>
<p>At the latest refinancing credit auction, the central bank's one-week rate was 53 percent.</p>
<p>Details on issues:</p>
<p>    Official    Issue     Maturity     T-bills on offer</p>
<p>    Code	  Date	 Date	    (bln lei)</p>
<p>    1997-A2     Jan 9	Apr 10	   534.37</p>
<p>    1997-F3     Jan 9	Apr 10	    78.9</p>
<p>    1997-H1     Jan 10     Apr 17	   380.0</p>
<p>    1997-C1     Jan 16     Apr 17	   184.0</p>
<p>    1997-H2     Jan 17     Apr 24	   501.0</p>
<p>    1997-F4     Jan 23     May 8	    183.8</p>
<p>    1997-D1     Jan 30     May 8	    300.16</p>
<p>    1997-H3     Jan 24     May 15	   503.1</p>
<p>NOTE: The T-bills may be bought by commercial banks operating in Romania and their corporate clients.</p>
<p>($=4,143 lei)</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
